[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: Chigorin Defense, 3...dxc4"]
[ECO "D07"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "regain-the-pawn,isolated-pawn"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3...dxc4"]
[Start "chigorin 3.Nf3"]

3... dxc4 { Takes the pawn. This is the same position as the Queen's Gambit Accepted with 3...Nc6. } 4. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1, which takes back on c4. The knight on c6 blocks Black's c-pawn, so ...b5 is hard to support. } 4... e5 ( 4... Bg4 5. Bxc4 e6 6. Nc3 { Develops and guards e4. Black's bishop on g4 can be asked with h3 later. } ) ( 4... Nf6 5. Bxc4 ) 5. Bxc4 { Pawn regained. If Black takes on d4, White takes back with the e-pawn and has open lines for the pieces. } 5... exd4 ( 5... Bb4+ 6. Nc3 exd4 7. exd4 ) 6. exd4 Bb4+ ( 6... Nf6 7. O-O ) 7. Nc3 Nf6 8. O-O O-O 9. h3 { Stops ...Bg4, which would pin the knight that guards d4. Plan: Bg5 or Re1, and push d5 when it chases the knight on c6. } *
